Skill: Comment back on the originating `${scenario_request_label}` issue with the Cursor agent's verdict. The PR itself is created upstream by the Cursor Cloud Agent's GitHub App (`OpenAsCursorGithubApp = true`, `autoCreatePr = true`) — this skill ONLY covers the final `gh issue comment` posted via the GitHub Guild integration.

Keywords for skill discovery: gh issue comment, scenario-request, issue reply, cursor verdict, scaffolded a PR, draft PR, existing scenario match, workflow blocked, guild spend cap, Cursor platform billing, cursor_platform_cap.

Prerequisites (all from notes, populated upstream):
- `repository_full_name`, `issue_or_pr_number` — for the `--repo` and target args.
- `gate_result` — `pass` (continue) or `wrong_repo` / `missing_label` (skip; gate-fail comment was already posted in `analyze-issue` via Template F).
- `cursor_verdict` — `match` | `pr` | `draft_pr` | `blocked`. Set by the cursor-author subagent after parsing the `cursor_agents_run_task` response (see orchestration SOP §3 for the canonical note keys).
- `cursor_pr_url` — set when `cursor_verdict ∈ {pr, draft_pr}`.
- `cursor_match_name` — set when `cursor_verdict == match`.
- `cursor_summary` — one-paragraph excerpt from Cursor's conversation summary (the `## Verdict` block plus the surrounding rationale lines).
- `cursor_platform_cap` — optional note key `"true"` when §6(c) detected **Cursor SaaS** billing / quota / account limits (distinct from StackGen `agent_budget`).
- `stage_summary:*` — any stage that recorded `blocked: <reason>` or `guild_spend_cap_reached` (Guild planner USD cap — exact substring).

Tool boundary: every command here runs in the GitHub Guild integration sandbox via the `notify-issue-comment` subagent (orchestration SOP Template E). `gh issue comment` authenticates via the integration's pre-bound PAT (orchestration SOP §0a). NO token threading. NO Ubuntu CLI sandbox is provisioned by this module — the legacy `git push` / `gh pr create` flow has moved into Cursor.

========================================================================
0) Sanity gate
========================================================================

a) `read_notes` for `gate_result`. If `gate_result != "pass"`, the gate-fail comment was already posted in `analyze-issue`; SKIP everything below and `note stage_summary:notify-issue-comment="skipped: gate-fail comment already posted"`.

b) Otherwise `read_notes` for `cursor_verdict`, `cursor_pr_url`, `cursor_match_name`, `cursor_summary`, `cursor_platform_cap` (if present), and every `stage_summary:*` key.

========================================================================
1) Pick exactly one comment body (first match wins)
========================================================================

Evaluate in order. The orchestration SOP's Template E enforces the same priority — keep the two in sync.

a) `read_notes` shows `cursor_platform_cap == "true"` OR (`cursor_verdict == "blocked"` AND (`cursor_summary` OR any `stage_summary:*` contains case-insensitive `insufficient account budget`, `cursor platform`, `billing`, `payment required`, or `quota exceeded`) AND `cursor_pr_url` is empty) → §2(a) "**Cursor platform temporarily unavailable**" (Cursor account / billing / quota — **not** StackGen `agent_budget`).
b) `cursor_verdict == "match"` → §2(b) "Existing scenario match".
c) ANY `stage_summary:*` contains the exact substring `guild_spend_cap_reached` AND `cursor_pr_url` is empty → §2(c) "**Guild planner budget exhausted**" (StackGen daily USD cap on this agent — `agent_budget`).
d) `cursor_verdict == "blocked"` OR ANY `stage_summary:*` begins with `blocked:` → §2(d) "Workflow blocked" (generic Cursor failure, gh auth, etc. — **only** if (a) did not already match).
e) `cursor_verdict == "pr"` AND `cursor_pr_url` non-empty → §2(e) "Scaffolded a PR".
f) `cursor_verdict == "draft_pr"` AND `cursor_pr_url` non-empty → §2(f) "Draft PR (validation failed)".
g) Else → §2(g) "Triaged, no action taken".

========================================================================
2) Comment body templates
========================================================================

a) Cursor platform / billing / quota (short-term Cursor SaaS limits):

```md
## Cursor platform temporarily unavailable

The automated scaffold step uses a **Cursor Cloud Agent** (separate from this
Guild's StackGen `agent_budget`). Cursor refused to launch the cloud agent:

> <verbatim excerpt from `cursor_summary` — usually billing, account budget, quota, or rate limit>

**What to do**

1. **Retry later** — Cursor account limits often reset hourly or daily; close
   and re-open this issue (or remove and re-add the \`${scenario_request_label}\`
   label) once credits/quota refresh.
2. **Operator:** confirm the Cursor API key / org has spend headroom in the
   Cursor dashboard (this is **not** fixed by raising \`agent_budget\` alone on
   the Terraform module — that cap only covers Guild planner LLM/tool spend).
3. **Manual fallback:** a scenario owner from \`CONTRIBUTORS-SE.md\` can scaffold
   from \`examples/scenarios/aws-sre-demo/\` and open a normal PR; see
   \`docs/se-feedback.md\`.

The bot will pick this issue up again on the next qualifying webhook event.
```

b) Existing-scenario match body:

```md
## Existing scenario match

The Cursor agent thinks `<cursor_match_name>` already covers this request.
Rationale (from Cursor's verdict block):

> <one-line "Reason:" excerpt from cursor_summary>

Run it now:
\`\`\`bash
make demo SCENARIO=<cursor_match_name>
\`\`\`

README: <https://github.com/${repository_full_name}/blob/<repository_default_branch>/examples/scenarios/<cursor_match_name>/README.md>

If this is wrong, comment with `not-a-match` and re-open / re-label — the
bot will re-triage on the next event.
```

c) Guild planner budget exhausted (StackGen `sg_agent_budget` / `agent_budget`):

```md
## Guild planner budget exhausted

This Guild agent hit its **StackGen daily USD cap** (\`agent_budget\` on the
\`aios-agent-scenario-author\` module) before it could finish planner work.

Recovery (any one of):

1. Wait for the UTC day boundary reset, then re-open / re-label this issue.
2. Ask the operator to raise \`agent_budget\` on the module instance if this
   happens often.
3. Manual scaffold: \`examples/scenarios/aws-sre-demo/\` + \`CONTRIBUTORS-SE.md\`.

Originating stage: \`<stage_id from the stage_summary containing guild_spend_cap_reached>\`.
```

d) Workflow-blocked body:

```md
## Workflow blocked

The scenario-author bot could not finish this request. Blocker (verbatim
from the Cursor agent's verdict block, or the upstream stage_summary):

> <quoted blocker text — `cursor_summary` when verdict==blocked, otherwise the matching stage_summary value>

<if cursor_summary mentions "Unknown modules:" — append:>
Modules the bot did not recognize from the issue body: `<comma-separated unknown_modules>`.
Either correct the names (see `modules/aios-*/` for valid names) or wait
for the modules to land, then re-open this issue.

Recovery: see `docs/se-feedback.md` and re-open this issue once the blocker
is fixed. The bot will re-triage when the next `issue.created` /
`issues.opened` / `issues.labeled` event fires (close + re-open with the
`${scenario_request_label}` label is the simplest way).
```

e) Happy-path PR body:

```md
## Scaffolded a PR

The Cursor agent opened a PR with the new scenario:

PR: <cursor_pr_url>

Validation: <Validation: line excerpt from cursor_summary>

## What's in the PR

<bullet list extracted from the "Files staged:" line of cursor_summary, grouped by directory>

Reviewer: please run `make demo SCENARIO=<derived from PR title or cursor_summary>`
against a clean tenant once you wire your credentials in
`terraform.tfvars`. The full reviewer checklist lives in the PR body.

<if cursor_summary mentions "Unknown modules:" — append:>
TODO before merge: `<comma-separated unknown modules from cursor_summary>` referenced in the issue did not match any module in `modules/`; the bot left them out — please add or rename.
```

f) Draft-PR body:

```md
## Scaffolded a draft PR (validation failed)

The Cursor agent opened a draft PR; `tofu validate` did not pass inside
its sandbox.

PR (draft): <cursor_pr_url>
Validation: <Validation: line excerpt from cursor_summary>

A scenario owner from `CONTRIBUTORS-SE.md` should review the validation
error and fix the scaffold before un-drafting. The PR body has the full
reviewer checklist. The bot does not have an ownership map, so it cannot
@-mention the right person here — please assign manually.
```

g) "Triaged, no action taken" body:

```md
## Triaged, no action taken

The scenario-author bot reached this issue but did not produce a PR, find
an existing match, or report a clear blocker. This usually means the
Cursor agent yielded mid-task (transient error or sandbox timeout).

Recovery: close and re-open this issue (the bot re-triages on the next
`issue.created` event) or wait — the workflow will fire again on any
future event. If this is the second consecutive "no action taken" reply,
please ping the engineering lead in `#solutions-se`.
```

========================================================================
3) Post the comment
========================================================================

ONE call via `${github_tool_prefix}_execute_command`:

```
gh issue comment <issue_or_pr_number> --repo <repository_full_name> --body-file - <<'EOF'
<body from §2>
EOF
```

After the comment:
- `note key="final_comment_url"`, value=`<best-effort URL>` (parse from `gh issue comment` output if available; otherwise emit `https://github.com/<repository_full_name>/issues/<issue_or_pr_number>`).
- `note key="final_comment_kind"`, value=one of `wrong_repo` | `missing_label` | `existing_match` | `cursor_platform_cap` | `guild_spend_cap` | `blocked` | `happy_pr` | `draft_pr` | `no_action`.
- `note key="stage_summary:notify-issue-comment"`, value=one paragraph: chosen comment kind + the issue URL.

Forbidden:
- Posting any secret value in any comment.
- Sending more than one comment per workflow run (Template E runs at most once).
- Re-running `${cursor_tool_prefix}_cursor_agents_run_task` from this stage — Cursor's task already finished upstream; this stage is comment-only.
- Capturing or persisting a `gh_token` (auth is pre-provisioned — see orchestration SOP §0a).
- Force-pushing or pushing branches — branch + push + PR is Cursor's GitHub App's job, not ours.
